+const _relayUrls = ['ws://localhost:8080', 'ws://localhost:7777'];
+
+bool _rustBridgeInitialized = false;
+
+/// Resets the backend so each test starts from a clean, logged-out state. The
+/// bundled `all_tests.dart` entrypoint runs every test in one process:
+/// `RustLib` (the FFI bridge) initialises once, while `deleteAllData` clears
+/// the process-global Whitenoise instance — which must then be re-installed
+/// with a fresh `initializeWhitenoise`, per that API's documented contract.
+Future<void> _resetBackend() async {
+  if (_rustBridgeInitialized) {
+    await rust_api.deleteAllData();
+  } else {
+    await RustLib.init();
+    _rustBridgeInitialized = true;
+  }
+
+  final root = await Directory.systemTemp.createTemp('whitenoise_integration_');
+  final dataDir = Directory('${root.path}/data');
+  final logsDir = Directory('${root.path}/logs');
+  await dataDir.create(recursive: true);
+  await logsDir.create(recursive: true);

comment.body:
_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Clean up per-test temp directories after each mount.**

Line 34 creates a fresh temp root per test, but there is no teardown that removes it. Over repeated runs this leaks disk state and can destabilize integration environments.


<details>
<summary>💡 Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
-Future<void> _resetBackend() async {
+Future<Directory> _resetBackend() async {
   if (_rustBridgeInitialized) {
     await rust_api.deleteAllData();
   } else {
     await RustLib.init();
     _rustBridgeInitialized = true;
   }
@@
   final config = await rust_api.createWhitenoiseConfig(
     dataDir: dataDir.path,
     logsDir: logsDir.path,
     defaultRelayUrls: _relayUrls,
   );
   await rust_api.initializeWhitenoise(config: config);
+  return root;
 }
@@
 Future<ProviderContainer> mountApp(WidgetTester tester) async {
-  await _resetBackend();
+  final root = await _resetBackend();
@@
   addTearDown(container.dispose);
+  addTearDown(() async {
+    if (await root.exists()) {
+      await root.delete(recursive: true);
+    }
+  });
```
</details>


Also applies to: 50-70

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@integration_test/_support/app_setup.dart` around lines 34 - 38, The temp
directories created by Directory.systemTemp.createTemp (variables root, dataDir,
logsDir) are not removed after each test, causing disk leaks; update the test
setup in app_setup.dart to register a teardown that recursively deletes root
(thereby removing dataDir and logsDir) after each mount—either by returning the
root Directory from the setup function and calling root.delete(recursive: true)
in a finally block or by calling the test framework's teardown hook (e.g.,
addTearDown) to perform root.delete(recursive: true); apply the same cleanup for
the other temp roots created in the 50-70 range.
```

</details>

