+  }

   fail('Timed out returning to the chat list');
 }
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@integration_test/_support/app_flows.dart` around lines 235 - 255, The
function returnToChatList uses a fixed attempt loop (attempt < 8) which is
brittle; change it to a timeout-based loop (e.g., track a start timestamp and
loop while elapsed < timeout such as 10 seconds) so it keeps pumping and
checking until either find.byKey(Key('chat_add_button')) is present or the
timeout expires; inside the loop keep the existing checks for
find.byKey(Key('back_button')) and find.byKey(Key('slate_back_button')) and
await tester.tap(...) when found, and on timeout call fail('Timed out returning
to the chat list'). Ensure you reference and update the returnToChatList
function and keep the same key identifiers ('chat_add_button', 'back_button',
'slate_back_button') while replacing the fixed-attempt logic with elapsed-time
checking.
```

</details>

