_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Handle errors for unawaited analytics callbacks.**

Line 425 and Line 426 launch async work with `unawaited(...)`, but failures from `resolveAnalyticsNotice()` (notably `markResolved`) can bubble as unhandled async errors. Wrap these paths with explicit error handling (either inside the async methods or via `.catchError(...)`) so notice actions cannot emit uncaught exceptions.


<details>
<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
 Future<void> resolveAnalyticsNotice() async {
   final resolutionService = ref.read(analyticsOnboardingResolutionServiceProvider);
   final resolvedProvider = analyticsOnboardingResolvedProvider(pubkey);
   if (!context.mounted) return;
   analyticsStepResolved.value = true;
-  await resolutionService.markResolved(pubkey);
+  try {
+    await resolutionService.markResolved(pubkey);
+  } catch (_) {
+    return;
+  }
   if (!context.mounted) return;
   ref.invalidate(resolvedProvider);
 }
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@lib/screens/chat_list_screen.dart` around lines 425 - 426, The unawaited
calls for onAnalyticsDismiss and onAnalyticsShare can let exceptions from
resolveAnalyticsNotice() or shareAnalytics bubble as unhandled async errors;
wrap these calls with explicit error handling. Replace the current arrow-call
patterns with short async closures that await the call inside try/catch (e.g.
onAnalyticsDismiss: () async { try { await resolveAnalyticsNotice(); } catch (e,
s) { /* log or handle error */ } }) or append .catchError(...) to the futures
(e.g. unawaited(resolveAnalyticsNotice().catchError((e, s) { /* log */ }))), and
do the same for shareAnalytics to ensure failures are caught and logged.
```

</details>

